Engineering Dynamics — MIT 2.003SC, Fall 2011 (@mech-mit-dynamics: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mech-sources) { r_37MSK6EJHRV95GXWA23P4ZJPZ3
J. Kim Vandiver and David Gossard. [Course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-003sc-engineering-dynamics-fall-2011/) · [Resource index](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-003sc-engineering-dynamics-fall-2011/pages/resource-index/) · [Syllabus](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-003sc-engineering-dynamics-fall-2011/pages/syllabus/).

The undergraduate course supplies 27 lecture entries, recitations, problem sets and solutions, two quizzes and a final examination. Follow the whole available sequence progressively. The syllabus expects calculus, differential equations and introductory mechanics; the learning Records make that preparation explicit. Suggested commercial textbooks are not required by the syllabus and are not supplied here.

On 30 October 2026 the indexes, syllabus and selected written methods were inspected: [planar motion](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-003sc-engineering-dynamics-fall-2011/resources/mit2_003scf11_rec2notes1/), [cart and pendulum](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-003sc-engineering-dynamics-fall-2011/resources/mit2_003scf11_rec8notes1/), [frequency response](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-003sc-engineering-dynamics-fall-2011/resources/mit2_003scf11_rec10note1/) and [problem set 10 solutions](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-003sc-engineering-dynamics-fall-2011/resources/mit2_003scf11_pset10sol/). This was not a playback check of every video. Some units explicitly have no assignment or recitation.

[OCW terms](https://ocw.mit.edu/pages/privacy-and-terms-of-use/) identify CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with component notices. All files and media remain external references.

**Return:** [Mechanical-engineering sources](../Sources.lingua#r_06RZYPZEFNMZ6MZ690QB1WN1Z2).
